# /etc/rc: the services init starts (kernel/user/init.c), one a line:
# once|respawn PATH ARGS...
#
# The desktop: the display server, which takes the screen, the keyboard
# and the pointer and serves Wayland clients at /run/wayland-0, the logo
# key starting a terminal; the panel along the top of the screen, which
# starts a terminal running the shell when no window is shown (#185); a
# login on the console, the UART, started again when its session ends, and
# shd, a login and a shell for each TCP connection to port 23. Nothing here
# ends the machine: it runs until it is stopped.
respawn /bin/compositor -l /bin/term
respawn /bin/panel /bin/term
respawn /bin/login
respawn /bin/shd
